```sql
-- Description / thinking process:
-- 1. Identify each individual pick line: picking_line has (picklist_id, line_no) as its natural key.
-- 2. Connect that pick to the physical stock it was taken from:
--      • Same location_id (rack/bin) and same product_id must match an inventory row.
-- 3. The inventory row stores purchase_id; by joining to purchases we obtain the
--    original purchase date, which is how FIFO is determined.
-- 4. Columns selected:
--      • picklist_id, line_no        → uniquely identify the pick line
--      • order_id, product_id, qty   → what was picked
--      • inventory.qty               → how much is currently left in that lot
--      • purchases.purchased         → when that lot was first received
-- 5. Order results by earliest purchase date (FIFO) and, within the same date,
--    by inventory.qty so that the “smallest‑available‑qty first” preference is visible.
-- 6. LIMIT 20 to keep the output concise.
SELECT pl.picklist_id,
       pl.line_no,
       pl.order_id,
       pl.product_id,
       pl.qty          AS pick_qty,
       i.qty           AS inventory_qty_now,
       pu.purchased    AS purchase_date
FROM   picking_line AS pl
JOIN   inventory    AS i  ON i.location_id = pl.location_id
                          AND i.product_id  = pl.product_id
JOIN   purchases    AS pu ON pu.id = i.purchase_id
ORDER  BY pu.purchased,
         i.qty
LIMIT 20;
```
